@startuml notifications-flow
title Notifications - Domain Events to Staff In-App and Email

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
  BorderColor #B45309
}

actor "Staff actor" as staff
participant "Emitting context\nroute or CLI job" as emitter
participant "notifications.public\nNotificationDispatcher" as dispatcher
database "notifications table" as store
participant "Identity published language" as identity
participant "Email sender" as email
participant "Angular topbar / notifications UI" as ui

emitter -> dispatcher : notify() / notify_many()
dispatcher -> identity : resolve target PermissionId(s)
identity --> dispatcher : staff permissions + user emails
dispatcher -> store : create Notification\nrecipient_permission_id\nrelated_resource_type / _id / _label
emitter -> email : send e-mail after commit,\nwhere the event has a template

note over emitter, email
  **Kinds and who emits them**

  use_of_collections.proposal_routes
    PROPOSAL_SUBMITTED, PROPOSAL_ASSIGNED, PROPOSAL_FORWARDED,
    PROPOSAL_TAKEN_OVER, PROPOSAL_REFERRED_TO_DIRECTION,
    PROPOSAL_RETURNED_TO_STAFF, PROPOSAL_DOCUMENTS_SUBMITTED

  public_submission.routes
    PROPOSAL_SUBMITTED (after double opt-in materialisation),
    PROPOSAL_CORRECTIONS_SUBMITTED

  museum_questions
    MUSEUM_QUESTION_SUBMITTED, MUSEUM_QUESTION_FORWARDED,
    MUSEUM_QUESTION_RESPONSE_OVERDUE (notify-overdue CLI job)

  scientific_return
    SCIENTIFIC_RETURN_CANDIDATES_FOUND
    (run-watch route, and the run-due / agentic-queue jobs)

  RelatedResourceType is PROPOSAL, PROJECT or MUSEUM_QUESTION.
  E-mail is a separate channel: approval, rejection and project
  start/complete/cancel e-mail the requester without writing an
  in-app notification.
end note

staff -> ui : open authenticated workspace
ui -> store : GET /api/v1/notifications/unread-count
store --> ui : unread count
ui -> store : GET /api/v1/notifications\nunreadOnly?, page, size
store -> identity : hydrate triggered_by label
identity --> store : PermissionView
store --> ui : paginated notifications

staff -> ui : mark one read
ui -> store : POST /api/v1/notifications/{id}/read
store --> ui : updated NotificationResponse

staff -> ui : mark all / clear all
ui -> store : POST /api/v1/notifications/read-all\nor /clear-all
store --> ui : affected count

@enduml
